"""SmartDecline PCMCI validation, release 1.1.0 (2026-10-01).

Analysis code is identical to version 3.2.0, with which the manuscript's
validation results were produced; release 1.1.0 adds only outputs:
  V1_wave_distribution_all_strata.csv   (Supplementary Table S1, panel b)
  V2_common_set.csv: row "own lag only"  (Supplementary Table S2, panel b)
  V9_figure4_lines.json, V9_figure4_quintile_slopes.csv (input to make_figure4.py)
  V9_dose_response_region.csv            (region robustness, Table 8 note)
All previously existing outputs are unchanged for a given seed.

Standalone (no complete_pipeline import).  Design principle: the primary
specification reproduces the manuscript EXACTLY (Gate 1 on Table 1, Gate 2/3
on Tables 5-7 when `networks` runs); every methodological refinement proposed
in v2.0.0 is kept as an explicit, switchable ROBUSTNESS layer, so that each
validation statistic is attached to the numbers the reviewers actually see.

Primary specification (== manuscript / complete_pipeline.py v1.0.x)
  --window lag1        transition mask on lag-1 pairs (same respondent,
                       consecutive years); Tigramite array construction is
                       replicated exactly, including the lag-2 source-parent
                       conditions of the MCI stage.
  movers included      cluster membership of a transition = municipality at t.
  statistic 'paper'    model-specific MCI, Fisher z with n-3 (Table 7).

Robustness layers
  --window strict3     t, t-1, t-2 consecutive for the same respondent in ALL
                       stages (v2 proposal).  `window_check` reports the target
                       coefficients under BOTH windows without changing the
                       primary tables.
  --exclude-movers     drop respondents observed in >1 municipality.
  statistic 'union'    both subsets re-estimated under the union of their MCI
                       conditioning sets (R1 Major 2, first point).
  --label-blocks       global | region | prefecture, comma-separated; V6 runs
                       each mode and reports block diagnostics (number of
                       mixed blocks, log10 distinct assignments).

Steps
  gate        Table 1 reproduction (hard stop unless --force)
  networks    all pooled / within / pooled_T3plus models (24 + 12), Gate 2/3
  diag        V1 wave counts, rho_within, iid heuristic, MCI, own-lag MCI
  common      V2 own / union / bivariate sets, both statistics
  boot        V4 municipality block bootstrap on the aligned design
  ahiv        V5 Anderson-Hsiao IV (year FE and COVID-difference)
  perm_time   V3 within-person time permutation (S, N and All replicates)
  perm_label  V6 municipality label permutation, per --label-blocks mode
  window_check V7 target coefficients under the other window
  period_check V8 target coefficient by transition position (first vs later)
               and by calendar year, conditioning sets held fixed
  dose        V9 continuous moderation by the municipal population change rate
               (within OLS with own lag + year FE, cluster SE, randomisation
               inference, Anderson-Hsiao IV, quintile profile); 65+ and 15-64
  dose_extra  V9 figure inputs and region robustness only (no randomisation
               re-run of V9; a few minutes)

Families for selection adjustment (frozen here, see FAMILIES):
  single (the pre-identified edge), CS13 (E3: Caregiving Support as source),
  care50 (Caregiving or Parenting Support as source or target), all182,
  and the manuscript's own selection rule (edges reported in the shrinking
  model).  Permutation p-values are (b+1)/(B+1).

Usage
  python validation_analysis.py --xlsx workbook.xlsx --outdir validation \
      --steps gate,diag,common,boot,ahiv,perm_time,perm_label,window_check,period_check,dose \
      --nboot 2000 --nrep-time 500 --nrep-label 500 --seed 2026

Repeating the same command resumes cached fits and replicates.  Separate calls
per scale merge tables by key.  Only aggregate outputs are written.

Parallel workers (local machine): launch several processes with disjoint
--rep-range slices (e.g. 0:125, 125:250, ...) for the same step/scale/mode;
each writes its own replicate checkpoints and no summary.  A final run of the
same command WITHOUT --rep-range reads all checkpoints and writes the summary.
"""
